course: dictionary
lesson: 4051
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and «generation» is a good example. The words around it show you which meaning fits. Read the whole sentence, then ask: which meaning makes sense here?
explain: Sometimes a generation is a group of people or animals born at about the same time. «Over many generations» means across many of these groups, over a long time. In the finch story, the birds' beaks changed over many generations, not in one year.
explain: Sometimes generation means the time it takes children to grow up and have children of their own, about 25 to 30 years. In science, power generation means making electricity from wind, sun or water. A new generation of a phone is a newer version of it.
fact: A generation is all the people born and living at about the same time, like children, parents or grandparents.
fact: A generation can also mean about 25 to 30 years, the time it takes children to grow up and have children of their own.
fact: «Power generation» means making electricity, for example from wind, sun or water.
fact: «Passed down from generation to generation» means handed on from one family group to the next.
fact: A generation of a product is one version of it, like a newer model of a phone.
exercise: «Over many generations, birds whose beaks fitted the food survived better.» What does generation mean here? | A new version of a phone | *Groups of animals born at about the same time | Making electricity from wind | A shop that sells seeds
exercise: In science, «power generation» means what? | Drawing a family tree | *Making electricity from wind, sun or water | Counting the people in a family | Choosing which animals have babies
exercise: «Passed down from generation to generation» means what? | *Handed on from one family group to the next | Written in a new language | Shared only once | Lost forever in a box
test: Ella says a generation is always exactly one year. Is she right? | *No, it is about 25 to 30 years for children to grow up and have children | No, it is a type of phone | Yes, one year exactly | Yes, but only for animals
test: «Changing an animal by choosing which ones have babies shows how much living things can change over many generations.» What does generations mean here? | A shop for animals | *Groups of living things born one after another over a long time | A family tree drawn on paper | A single day
exam: Which sentence uses generation to mean a new version of a product? | Birds changed over many generations | Power generation uses wind and sun | *The next generation of phones has a bigger screen | The younger generation visited their grandparents
